entries.description:
The number of plankton in a tank is doubling every 5 days, given by the formula:
P = 15000 × 2^{t/5}
Where P is population (number of plankton) after t days from commencement of study.

The mass, in grams, of a decaying substance is given by
M = 18 × (1.75)^{-3t/5}
Where t is measured in days.
